{"seq":31,"at":"2026-10-23","kind":"edited","target":{"type":"article","id":"a0980"},"reason":"The sentence on the Aten, the sun disc briefly worshipped as Egypt's sole god, now explains Akhenaten's change of name, the Amarna period (c. 1353–1336 BC) and the new capital, so the new Aten question has its sentence.","by":"fact-count-rework","changes":[{"field":"bodyEn","diff":[["=",366],["-","god."],["+","god of the state: the pharaoh, born Amenhotep IV, took the name Akhenaten to proclaim his bond with the disc and, in the Amarna period of about 1353–1336 BC, built it a new capital at Amarna, a cult that did not outlive him."],["=",816]]},{"field":"bodyDe","diff":[["=",354],["-","verehrt."],["+","des Staates verehrt: Der Pharao, als Amenophis IV. geboren, nahm den Namen Echnaton an, um seine Verbindung mit der Scheibe zu verkünden, und erbaute ihr in der Amarnazeit um 1353–1336 v. Chr. eine neue Hauptstadt in Amarna – ein Kult, der ihn nicht überlebte."],["=",794]]},{"field":"bodyRu","diff":[["=",314],["-","бог."],["+","бог государства: фараон, рождённый Аменхотепом IV, принял имя Эхнатон, чтобы возвестить свою связь с диском, и в амарнский период, около 1353–1336 годов до н. э., построил ему новую столицу в Амарне — культ, который не пережил своего создателя."],["=",732]]}],"hash":"75f7a31ea135"},
